# Save context in the repo

Diana may lose Cursor account access at any time. **Do not rely on** personal Cursor skills (`~/.cursor/skills/`), the personal agent store, or chat-only memory for anything this project needs again.

## Where to write

| Kind | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Reusable workflows | `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (+ scripts/reference alongside) |
| Standing conventions | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Brand, pricing, ops notes | `docs/` (e.g. `docs/pricing/`) |
| Index for agents | `.cursor/README.md` |

## When to save

- After a new workflow, decision, or convention emerges in chat → add or update a skill, rule, or doc in the repo in the same session when practical.
- When copying from `~/.cursor/skills/` → put the full copy in `.cursor/skills/` and point scripts/docs at **repo-relative paths** (from project root).
- When creating skills that only live in the personal folder → copy into this repo before treating the work as done.

## Do not

- Tell Diana to “check your personal skill at ~/.cursor/…” as the source of truth.
- Leave important context only in Cursor cloud or a single chat thread.

## Scripts

Prefer paths under this repo (e.g. `.cursor/skills/.../scripts/`). A fallback to `~/.cursor/skills/` is acceptable only for backward compatibility on her Mac, not as the primary documentation path.
